  <data name="CONVERTER_AREARASTER_DESCR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Convert GIS vector data to a Ecospace raster with polygon/cell area cell overlap ratios. For this, every cell area / polygon area overlap ratio is calculated, and the ratio [0, 1] is stored in the raster. This method becomes slow for large polygon data sets.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_AREARASTER_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Area ratios</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_COOKIECUTTER_DESCR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Convert GIS vector data to a Ecospace raster using the vector data as a mask, where either values inside or outside the vector data are rasterized.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_COOKIECUTTER_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Masked conversion</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_DIRECTRASTER_DESCR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Convert GIS raster or polygon data to a value raster compatible with Ecospace. Executed GIS raster operations are Clip and Resample.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_DIRECTRASTER_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Raster interpolation</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_DIRECTVECTOR_DESCR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Convert GIS vector data (points, multi-points and polygones) to a pesence/absence raster compatible with Ecospace, where a vector attribute is matched to the name of object in Ecospace</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_DIRECTVECTOR_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Presence/absence conversion</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_ISOBAR_DESCR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Convert GIS isobar (height contours) to a Ecospace depth map.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CONVERTER_ISOBAR_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Isobar conversion</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DATASET_ASCII_DESCRIPTION" xml:space="preserve">
